+// The bend happens in two clean stages, so the sheet never tears or passes through itself: first the flat sheet rolls up
+// (like paper round a tube, its middle staying in front), then the tube swells or pinches into the surface. All three
+// surfaces turn about the z-axis, so the rolled sheet's seam can sit at the back without changing the shape.
